## 3. Stage-by-Stage Mint-to Logic™ & Shepherd's Process Analysis

* **`[100]` Intake & Governed MCP Gateway Normalization:** Centralizes disparate tool endpoints and local credential files behind a single governed MCP Gateway endpoint, normalizing `tools/list` and `tools/call` traffic with attached JWT/IdP identity context.
* **`[200]` Validation / Cedar Policy & Parameter-Level Gate:** Evaluates natural-language-authored, Cedar-enforced policy rules (alongside optional Bedrock Guardrails checks for prompt injection and sensitive data leakage) against principal identity claims, environment tags, and tool input parameters in the request path before any backend tool executes—mirroring deterministic pre-execution validation and trigger gating.
* **`[300]` Mint Unit / Isolated MicroVM Session & Scoped Token Context:** Pairs per-session Cognito/JWT bearer tokens with isolated AgentCore Runtime microVM sessions (up to 8 hours) and auditable episodic memory—mirroring session-level containment and identity binding without constructing a cryptographic Mint Unit Container with hash/timestamp/routing-directive/commit fields.
* **`[400]` Routing / Gateway Target & Interceptor Dispatch:** Routes validated tool calls across registered MCP targets, YAML-manifested external tools, and ordered request/response interceptors—mirroring policy-conditioned dispatch without branching into Burn, Limbo, Access, or Code protocol states.
* **`[500a]` Burn / Session Tear-Down & Credential Non-Exposure:** Keeps backend credentials sealed inside AWS KMS / Secrets Manager so they never leave the boundary, revokes session tokens, and tears down isolated microVM sessions upon completion—mirroring credential isolation and session cleanup without executing an authorization-gated single-use credential burn on a discrete mint unit.
* **`[500b]` Limbo / Threshold Escalation & Human-in-the-Loop Hold:** Supports policy thresholds that auto-approve low-risk parameters while halting high-risk parameters for human approval (paired with circuit-breaker blast-radius controls and guardrail interceptors)—mirroring conditional hold-and-escalation logic, though implemented via Cedar rule gates rather than an autonomous Mint Unit expiration and auto-burn timer.
* **`[500c]` Access / RBAC, ABAC & Proxy Egress Lockdown:** Enforces default-deny Cedar RBAC/ABAC access rules on tool and parameter invocations, blocks non-gateway MCP traffic at the corporate proxy/EDR, and constrains web search to zero-data-egress managed endpoints—representing one of the strongest enterprise parallels to strict access and egress containment.
* **`[500d]` Code / Isolated Sandbox & Tool-Gateway Execution:** Executes agent-generated code and shell commands inside isolated microVM sandboxes (Strands Shell) and routes external tool calls through the governed MCP Gateway—mirroring contained code/tool execution boundaries.
* **`[600]` Audit / Deny Logs, Continuous Evaluators & Episodic Memory Audit:** Captures every gateway allow/deny decision in CloudWatch, guardrail intervention spikes, cost anomalies, episodic memory entries, and 13 continuous evaluator scores—providing structured compliance auditability across agent runs.

